# Clean stale build artifacts after commit

After **every successful `git commit`**, run:

```bash
python3 scripts/clean_old_artifacts.py
```

## What counts as an artifact (only if mtime older than 7 days)

- Under `exports/`, `data/`
- `__pycache__/`, `.pytest_cache/`, `.mypy_cache/`, `dist/`, `build/`
- `*.artrans`, `*.artrans.json`, `*.pyc`, `*.pyo`, `*.log`, `.DS_Store`

## Never delete

- Source: `deploy/`, `scripts/`, `.cursor/rules/`, `.env.example`
- Secrets: `.env`, `.ssh/`
- Anything newer than 7 days

## Automation already wired

- Cursor: `.cursor/hooks.json` → `afterShellExecution` matcher `git commit`
- Git: `scripts/git-hooks/post-commit` (copy to `.git/hooks/post-commit` after `git init`)

If the hook did not run (commit outside Cursor / hooks disabled), run the script yourself before finishing the turn.
